          "guid": "mt33im9y6y9t5og7",
          "message": {
            "text": "A repository-owned font with no materializable HarfBuzz face proves that failure stays candidate-local: the authored PUA range terminates on the original first candidate with first-candidate-notdef instead of entering legacy assignment. The focused Vitest command passed 50 tests with 4 platform skips, and the feature mutation separately proves every post-miss verdict probe carries -liga.",
            "markdown": "A repository-owned font with no materializable HarfBuzz face proves that failure stays candidate-local: the authored PUA range terminates on the original first candidate with first-candidate-notdef instead of entering legacy assignment. The focused Vitest command passed 50 tests with 4 platform skips, and the feature mutation separately proves every post-miss verdict probe carries -liga."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/cluster-fallback.test.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 131,
                  "endLine": 156,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "describe(\"candidate-local HarfBuzz materialization failure\", () => {\n  it(\"keeps FontFallbackIterator ownership instead of declining to a per-codepoint walk\", () => {\n    // A directly opened fixture has neither a registered source record nor a\n    // resolvable platform key, so Domotion's HarfBuzz bridge cannot materialize\n    // this first candidate. Blink's terminal still belongs to that first\n    // candidate; an implementation-wide legacy restart would change both the\n    // mechanism and the assignment algorithm.\n    const opened = fontkit.openSync(\"assets/fonts/fixture/DomotionFixtureSerif-Regular.ttf\");\n    const font = (\"fonts\" in opened\n      ? (opened as unknown as { fonts: Array<typeof opened> }).fonts[0]\n      : opened) as Parameters<typeof splitTextIntoFontRunsShaped>[1];\n    const text = \"\\uE000\";\n    const runs = splitTextIntoFontRunsShaped(\n      text, font, \"dm-unopenable\", 400, 32, 0, undefined, undefined,\n      [\"dm-unopenable\"], false, 100, undefined, \"DM Unopenable\",\n    );\n\n    expect(runs).toHaveLength(1);\n    expect(runs[0]).toMatchObject({\n      text,\n      startIdx: 0,\n      endIdx: 1,\n      fontKey: \"dm-unopenable\",\n      isPrimary: true,\n      routeMechanism: \"first-candidate-notdef\",\n    });"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
